pan style=3D"font-weight:700">So, does that mean Huang=E2=80=99s troubles a=
re officially over=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,s=
erif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Probably not. The board is continuin=
g to investigate, though it is an open question how vigorous that will be. =
Congress has summoned him to testify, and many lawmakers still have questio=
ns about his relationship with Alice Huang and whether it helped her compan=
y evade U.S. prohibitions on exporting Nvidia chips to China. There are eno=
ugh China hawks in both parties that some testimony is bound to happen, if =
not next week, then in the next Congress.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal=
 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-we=
ight:700">Do we know what sort of information Alice Huang</span><span>, </s=
pan><span style=3D"font-weight:700">who U.S. intelligence officials say was=
 a Chinese asset, passed on to the Chinese government over the years=3F</sp=
an></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 =
0 15px"><span>We know that Alice Huang had </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nyt=
